abstract: >
  SOX (Solvency & Information Integrity) is a formally specified audit framework
  for macroscopic phase stability. It establishes negative, veto-based criteria
  for the existence of coherent phases based on information solvency and
  incompatibility with volumetric noise. The framework is formally verified
  in Lean 4 and includes a canonical falsification protocol.
